# `grows-without-end`: a signed generic function that calls itself at `[a]` for `a`
# has no finite set of types (ruling PG; Type System ch. 2: recursion at another type
# needs the signature, and reaches finitely many types).
Depth: fn [a], Nat -> Nat
fn Depth xs, more = match more -? 1:
    ? less: Depth [[xs]], less
    nil: Len xs
